### What is a parallel stream?

A parallel stream splits data into partitions and processes them on multiple threads using the ForkJoinPool.

### How does it work internally?

```java
package com.bank.service;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.util.List;

public class ParallelDemo {
    record Transaction(String id, BigDecimal amount, boolean settled) {}

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Transaction> txns = List.of(
            new Transaction("TXN-001", new BigDecimal("45000"), true),
            new Transaction("TXN-002", new BigDecimal("78000"), true),
            new Transaction("TXN-003", new BigDecimal("12000"), false),
            new Transaction("TXN-004", new BigDecimal("250000"), true)
        );

        BigDecimal total = txns.parallelStream()
            .filter(Transaction::settled)
            .map(Transaction::amount)
            .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);

        System.out.println("Total: Rs." + total);
        System.out.println("Pool size: " + java.util.concurrent.ForkJoinPool.commonPool().getParallelism());
    }
}
```

